module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.DirectSum.Ring
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.GradedAlgebra.RingHom
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionProduct.PullbackUnitSection
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistTensor.PullbackSectionRing

/-!
# `ψ^d_φ` is a graded ring homomorphism

Let `S` be a graded ring, `X = Proj(S)`, `d` a positive natural number, `U_d` the degree `d` open
of Stacks Tag 01N5 and `φ : Y ⟶ U_d` a morphism of schemes. Stacks Tag 01N7 attaches to `φ` the
map

`ψ^d_φ : S^{(d)} ⟶ Γ_*(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(d))`

whose degree `n` component sends a homogeneous element of degree `nd` to the pullback along `φ` of
the global section of `𝒪_X(nd)` it defines, and asserts two things about it: that it is a graded
ring homomorphism, and that `φ⁎𝒪_X(d)` is globally generated by the image of degree one. This
file proves the twist-model form of the first, and states it together with the second,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.generatesStalks_psiPullbackVeroneseHom_one`.

The faithful form of Tag 01N7, with target the section ring `⨁_n Γ(Y, L^{⊗ n})` of Tag 01CV of
`L = φ⁎𝒪_{U_d}(d)`, is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackSectionRing_spec`
in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProjSectionRing`, and carries the tag.

The target is the graded commutative ring
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistTensor.veroneseSectionRing`: the direct sum of the section groups
`Γ(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(nd))`, multiplied by the pullback along `φ` of the canonical multiplication maps of
Stacks Tag 01MO read through the comparison of Stacks Tag 01CD. So the grading is by `n`, with
degree `n` piece the sections of the twist `φ⁎𝒪_X(nd)` itself rather than the sections of the
`n`-th tensor power of `φ⁎𝒪_X(d)`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.toProjRS`: the morphism of ringed spaces underlying
  `φ` followed by the inclusion `U_d ⟶ Proj(S)`, which is the morphism the twists are pulled back
  along.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackSumHom`: the ring homomorphism
  `⨁_n (S^{(d)})_n ⟶ Γ_*(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(d))` assembled from the degreewise maps.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullback`: **the graded ring homomorphism
  `ψ^d_φ : S^{(d)} ⟶ Γ_*(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(d))`.**

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackVeroneseHom_mul` and
  `psiPullbackVeroneseHom_one`: **the degreewise map is multiplicative and unital.** The product of
  two homogeneous elements of the Veronese subring is sent to the product of their images, and the
  unit to the unit section.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullback_apply_homogeneous`: on a homogeneous
  element of Veronese degree `n`, `ψ^d_φ` is the degree `n` component placed in the degree `n`
  summand.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullback_gradedRingHom_and_generatesStalks`:
  `ψ^d_φ` is a graded ring homomorphism into the twist model, and `φ⁎𝒪_X(d)` is globally
  generated by the image of degree one.

## Implementation notes

**Why `0 < d`.** `Stacks.Veronese.veroneseGradingGradedRing` takes it, because the decomposition
of the Veronese subring into the pieces `S_{nd}` needs `n ↦ nd` injective; this is the same
hypothesis `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjDegreeOpenSections.psi` takes.

**Universes.** The grading index type lives in the same universe as the ring.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Equation 01N7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N7)
* [Stacks Project, Equation 01N5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CD)
-/


@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction
open AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (degreeOpen)
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistSections
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistTensor
open Stacks.PullbackTensorCoherence (oneSec)
open Stacks.RingedSpace
open Stacks.Veronese
open scoped DirectSum

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj

universe u

variable {σ : Type u} {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] {Y : Scheme.{u}} {d : ℕ}

attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top
attribute [local implicit_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf sheafCompose

attribute [local instance] Stacks.PullbackGradedAlgebra.monoidalCategory
  Stacks.PullbackTensorCoherence.braidedCategory

/-- The morphism of ringed spaces underlying `φ` followed by the open immersion
`U_d ⟶ Proj(S)`: the morphism along which the twists of `Proj(S)` are pulled back. -/
abbrev toProjRS (φ : Y ⟶ (degreeOpen 𝒜 d).toScheme) :
    Y.toRingedSpace ⟶ (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜).toRingedSpace :=
  (toProj 𝒜 φ).toLRSHom.toShHom

/-- The degreewise map of `ψ^d_φ` is the pullback-unit image of the global section of `𝒪_X(nd)`
attached to the homogeneous element. -/
private theorem psiPullbackVeroneseHom_eq_pullbackUnit (φ : Y ⟶ (degreeOpen 𝒜 d).toScheme)
    (n : ℕ) (a : veroneseGrading 𝒜 d n) :
    psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ n a =
      pullbackUnit (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) (twist 𝒜 ((n * d : ℕ) : ℤ)) (op ⊤)
        (degreeSection 𝒜 (n * d) (veroneseToGrade 𝒜 d n a)) :=
  Stacks.PullbackUnitSection.pullbackSectionHom_top_eq (toProj 𝒜 φ)
    (twistingSheaf 𝒜 ((n * d : ℕ) : ℤ)) (by simp)
    (degreeSection 𝒜 (n * d) (veroneseToGrade 𝒜 d n a))

/-- Two global sections of the twists agree after transport along an equality of degrees as soon as
their values agree at every point. -/
private theorem eqToHom_twist_val_app_top_eq {d d' : ℤ} (h : d = d')
    (s : (twist 𝒜 d).val.obj (op ⊤)) (t : (twist 𝒜 d').val.obj (op ⊤))
    (H : ∀ z, s.1 z = t.1 z) : (eqToHom (congrArg (twist 𝒜) h)).val.app (op ⊤) s = t :=
  twist_section_ext 𝒜 (op ⊤) _ _ fun z => (eqToHom_twist_val_app_apply 𝒜 h (op ⊤) s z).trans (H z)

/-- The product of the global sections attached to two homogeneous elements of the Veronese
subring is the global section attached to their product, after the transport along
`nd + md = (n + m)d`. -/
private theorem eqToHom_mulSection_degreeSection (n m : ℕ) (a : veroneseGrading 𝒜 d n)
    (b : veroneseGrading 𝒜 d m) :
    (eqToHom (congrArg (twist 𝒜)
          (show ((n * d : ℕ) : ℤ) + ((m * d : ℕ) : ℤ) = (((n + m) * d : ℕ) : ℤ) from by
            push_cast; ring))).val.app (op (⊤ : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒜)))
        (mulSection 𝒜 ((n * d : ℕ) : ℤ) ((m * d : ℕ) : ℤ) (op ⊤)
          (degreeSection 𝒜 (n * d) (veroneseToGrade 𝒜 d n a))
          (degreeSection 𝒜 (m * d) (veroneseToGrade 𝒜 d m b))) =
      degreeSection 𝒜 ((n + m) * d)
        (veroneseToGrade 𝒜 d (n + m)
          (GradedMonoid.GMul.mul (A := fun i => (veroneseGrading 𝒜 d i : Type u)) a b)) := by
  refine eqToHom_twist_val_app_top_eq 𝒜 (by push_cast; ring) _ _ fun z => ?_
  refine Eq.trans (mulSection_apply 𝒜 ((n * d : ℕ) : ℤ) ((m * d : ℕ) : ℤ) (op ⊤)
    (degreeSection 𝒜 (n * d) (veroneseToGrade 𝒜 d n a))
    (degreeSection 𝒜 (m * d) (veroneseToGrade 𝒜 d m b)) z) ?_
  rw [degreeSection_apply, degreeSection_apply, degreeSection_apply]
  exact Eq.trans LocalizedModule.mk_mul_mk
    (congrArg (LocalizedModule.mk
      (((a : veroneseSubring 𝒜 d) : A) * ((b : veroneseSubring 𝒜 d) : A))) (mul_one 1))

/-- The global section attached to the unit of the Veronese subring is the image of the section
`1` of `𝒪_X` under the unit of the twists, after the transport along `0 = 0 · d`. -/
private theorem eqToHom_twistUnit_eq_degreeSection :
    (eqToHom (congrArg (twist 𝒜)
          (show (0 : ℤ) = ((0 * d : ℕ) : ℤ) from by push_cast; ring))).val.app
        (op (⊤ : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒜)))
        ((twistUnit 𝒜).val.app (op ⊤)
          (oneSec (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜).toRingedSpace (op ⊤))) =
      degreeSection 𝒜 (0 * d) (veroneseToGrade 𝒜 d 0 1) := by
  refine eqToHom_twist_val_app_top_eq 𝒜 (by push_cast; ring) _ _ fun z => ?_
  refine Eq.trans (twistUnit_val_app_apply 𝒜 (op ⊤)
    (oneSec (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜).toRingedSpace (op ⊤)) z) ?_
  rw [degreeSection_apply]
  exact Eq.trans HomogeneousLocalization.val_one (OreLocalization.one_def ..)

/-- **Stacks Project, Equation 27.12.0.3, multiplicativity.** The degreewise map of `ψ^d_φ`
carries the product of two homogeneous elements of the Veronese subring `S^{(d)}` to the product
of their images in the graded section ring of the pulled-back twists. -/
theorem psiPullbackVeroneseHom_mul (φ : Y ⟶ (degreeOpen 𝒜 d).toScheme) (n m : ℕ)
    (a : veroneseGrading 𝒜 d n) (b : veroneseGrading 𝒜 d m) :
    psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ (n + m)
        (GradedMonoid.GMul.mul (A := fun i => (veroneseGrading 𝒜 d i : Type u)) a b) =
      veroneseSectionMul 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤) n m
        (psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ n a) (psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ m b) := by
  refine Eq.trans (psiPullbackVeroneseHom_eq_pullbackUnit 𝒜 φ (n + m) _) ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg₂ (veroneseSectionMul 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤) n m)
    (psiPullbackVeroneseHom_eq_pullbackUnit 𝒜 φ n a).symm
    (psiPullbackVeroneseHom_eq_pullbackUnit 𝒜 φ m b).symm)
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (veroneseSectionMul_pullbackUnit 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d n m (op ⊤)
    (degreeSection 𝒜 (n * d) (veroneseToGrade 𝒜 d n a))
    (degreeSection 𝒜 (m * d) (veroneseToGrade 𝒜 d m b))).symm
  exact congrArg
    (pullbackUnit (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) (twist 𝒜 (((n + m) * d : ℕ) : ℤ)) (op ⊤))
    (eqToHom_mulSection_degreeSection 𝒜 n m a b).symm

/-- **Stacks Project, Equation 27.12.0.3, unitality.** The degreewise map of `ψ^d_φ` carries the
unit of the Veronese subring `S^{(d)}` to the unit section of the graded section ring of the
pulled-back twists. -/
theorem psiPullbackVeroneseHom_one (φ : Y ⟶ (degreeOpen 𝒜 d).toScheme) :
    psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ 0 1 =
      veroneseSectionOne 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤) := by
  refine Eq.trans (psiPullbackVeroneseHom_eq_pullbackUnit 𝒜 φ 0 1) ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (veroneseSectionOne_pullbackUnit 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)).symm
  exact congrArg (pullbackUnit (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) (twist 𝒜 ((0 * d : ℕ) : ℤ)) (op ⊤))
    (eqToHom_twistUnit_eq_degreeSection 𝒜).symm

/-- The degree `n` component of `ψ^d_φ`, with its target read as the degree `n` piece of the
graded section ring. -/
def psiPullbackSectionHom (φ : Y ⟶ (degreeOpen 𝒜 d).toScheme) (n : ℕ) :
    veroneseGrading 𝒜 d n →+ veroneseSections 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤) n :=
  psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ n

/-- `psiPullbackSectionHom` is `psiPullbackVeroneseHom`, retyped. -/
theorem psiPullbackSectionHom_apply (φ : Y ⟶ (degreeOpen 𝒜 d).toScheme) (n : ℕ)
    (a : veroneseGrading 𝒜 d n) :
    psiPullbackSectionHom 𝒜 φ n a = psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ n a := rfl

/-- The ring homomorphism `⨁_n (S^{(d)})_n ⟶ Γ_*(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(d))` assembled from the degreewise
maps. -/
def psiPullbackSumHom (φ : Y ⟶ (degreeOpen 𝒜 d).toScheme) :
    letI := veroneseSectionGradedRing 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)
    (⨁ n : ℕ, veroneseGrading 𝒜 d n) →+*
      veroneseSectionRing 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤) :=
  let := veroneseSectionGradedRing 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)
  DirectSum.toSemiring
    (fun n => (DirectSum.of (veroneseSections 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)) n).comp
      (psiPullbackSectionHom 𝒜 φ n))
    ((congrArg (DirectSum.of (veroneseSections 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)) 0)
        (psiPullbackVeroneseHom_one 𝒜 φ)).trans
      (DirectSum.one_def (veroneseSections 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤))).symm)
    (fun {n m} a b =>
      (congrArg (DirectSum.of (veroneseSections 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)) (n + m))
          (psiPullbackVeroneseHom_mul 𝒜 φ n m a b)).trans
        (DirectSum.of_mul_of
          (A := veroneseSections 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤))
          (psiPullbackSectionHom 𝒜 φ n a) (psiPullbackSectionHom 𝒜 φ m b)).symm)

/-- On a homogeneous summand the assembled ring map is the degreewise map. -/
theorem psiPullbackSumHom_of (φ : Y ⟶ (degreeOpen 𝒜 d).toScheme) (n : ℕ)
    (a : veroneseGrading 𝒜 d n) :
    letI := veroneseSectionGradedRing 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)
    psiPullbackSumHom 𝒜 φ
        (DirectSum.of (fun i => (veroneseGrading 𝒜 d i : Type u)) n a) =
      DirectSum.of (veroneseSections 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)) n
        (psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ n a) :=
  DirectSum.toAddMonoid_of
    (fun n => (DirectSum.of (veroneseSections 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)) n).comp
      (psiPullbackSectionHom 𝒜 φ n))
    n a

/-- **Stacks Project, Equation 27.12.0.3.** `ψ^d_φ : S^{(d)} ⟶ Γ_*(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(d))` is a graded ring
homomorphism from the `d`-th Veronese subring of `S` to the graded section ring of the pulled-back
twists `φ⁎𝒪_X(nd)`: a homogeneous element of degree `nd` is sent to the pullback along `φ` of the
global section of `𝒪_X(nd)` it determines, placed in the degree `n` summand. -/
def psiPullback (hd : 0 < d) (φ : Y ⟶ (degreeOpen 𝒜 d).toScheme) :
    letI := veroneseGradingGradedRing 𝒜 d hd
    letI := veroneseSectionGradedRing 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)
    veroneseGrading 𝒜 d →+*ᵍ veroneseSectionRingGrading 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤) :=
  let := veroneseGradingGradedRing 𝒜 d hd
  let := veroneseSectionGradedRing 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)
  { __ := (psiPullbackSumHom 𝒜 φ).comp
      (DirectSum.decomposeRingEquiv (veroneseGrading 𝒜 d)).toRingHom
    map_mem := fun {n x} hx =>
      ⟨psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ n ⟨x, hx⟩,
        (Eq.trans
          (congrArg (psiPullbackSumHom 𝒜 φ)
            (DirectSum.decompose_of_mem (veroneseGrading 𝒜 d) hx))
          (psiPullbackSumHom_of 𝒜 φ n ⟨x, hx⟩)).symm⟩ }

/-- On a homogeneous element of Veronese degree `n`, `ψ^d_φ` is the pullback along `φ` of the
global section of `𝒪_X(nd)` attached to it, placed in the degree `n` summand. -/
theorem psiPullback_apply_homogeneous (hd : 0 < d) (φ : Y ⟶ (degreeOpen 𝒜 d).toScheme) (n : ℕ)
    (a : veroneseGrading 𝒜 d n) :
    letI := veroneseGradingGradedRing 𝒜 d hd
    letI := veroneseSectionGradedRing 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)
    psiPullback 𝒜 hd φ (a : veroneseSubring 𝒜 d) =
      DirectSum.of (veroneseSections 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)) n
        (psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ n a) :=
  let := veroneseGradingGradedRing 𝒜 d hd
  let := veroneseSectionGradedRing 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)
  Eq.trans
    (congrArg (psiPullbackSumHom 𝒜 φ)
      (DirectSum.decompose_of_mem (veroneseGrading 𝒜 d) a.2))
    (psiPullbackSumHom_of 𝒜 φ n a)

/-! ### Equation 27.12.0.3 in the twist model -/

/-- **The twist-model form of Stacks Equation 27.12.0.3 (Tag 01N7).** Let `S` be a graded ring,
`X = Proj(S)`, let `d ≥ 1`, let `U_d ⊂ X` be the degree `d` open and let `φ : Y ⟶ U_d` be a
morphism of schemes. Then the degreewise maps assemble into a graded ring homomorphism

`ψ^d_φ : S^{(d)} ⟶ ⨁_n Γ(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(nd))`,

sending a homogeneous element of degree `nd` to the pullback along `φ` of the global section of
`𝒪_X(nd)` it determines, and the invertible sheaf `φ⁎𝒪_X(d)` is generated by the global sections
in the image of the degree-one component `(S^{(d)})_1 = S_d ⟶ Γ(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(d))`.

The target is the twist model of `Γ_*`: its degree `n` piece is `Γ(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(nd))` rather than
`Γ(Y, (φ⁎𝒪_X(d))^{⊗ n})`, and its product is the pullback of the twist multiplication maps. The
form of Tag 01N7 with target the section ring of Tag 01CV, multiplied through the tensor powers,
is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackSectionRing_spec`, which carries the
tag. The graded ring homomorphism of this declaration is available as `psiPullback`, and the two
conjuncts separately as `psiPullback_apply_homogeneous` and
`generatesStalks_psiPullbackVeroneseHom_one`. -/
theorem psiPullback_gradedRingHom_and_generatesStalks (hd : 0 < d)
    (φ : Y ⟶ (degreeOpen 𝒜 d).toScheme) :
    (letI := veroneseGradingGradedRing 𝒜 d hd
     letI := veroneseSectionGradedRing 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)
     ∃ ψ : veroneseGrading 𝒜 d →+*ᵍ veroneseSectionRingGrading 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤),
       ∀ (n : ℕ) (a : veroneseGrading 𝒜 d n),
         ψ (a : veroneseSubring 𝒜 d) =
           DirectSum.of (veroneseSections 𝒜 (toProjRS 𝒜 φ) d (op ⊤)) n
             (psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ n a)) ∧
      Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.GeneratesStalks
        (L := pullbackTwist 𝒜 φ ((1 * d : ℕ) : ℤ))
        (fun x : ↥(veroneseGrading 𝒜 d 1) => psiPullbackVeroneseHom 𝒜 φ 1 x) :=
  ⟨⟨psiPullback 𝒜 hd φ, psiPullback_apply_homogeneous 𝒜 hd φ⟩,
    generatesStalks_psiPullbackVeroneseHom_one 𝒜 φ⟩

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj

end
